insert into public.tips (id, unit_id, title_en, body_md, status) values
  ('041f794e-e18f-579b-99d7-01a95bf079bd', '00142c01-014f-53a8-b11d-1cf2bf832643', 'Paro docente, paro general', 'A strike is named after who stops: **paro docente** — *the teachers*; **paro de colectivos** — the **colectiveros**; **paro general** — everyone. The **gremio** — *the union* — **anunció un paro** for Thursday, and the news calls it a **medida de fuerza**.', 'draft'),
  ('ee61df72-edc1-551c-8a85-ffd52d0c70ad', '00142c01-014f-53a8-b11d-1cf2bf832643', '¿Funciona o no?', 'The morning after, the question is what still runs: **el subte funciona con normalidad**, or **suspendieron el servicio**. **Hubo un apagón** — *there was a blackout* — and the traffic lights are out: **embotellamiento**, **desvíos**, and half the city goes **a pie**.', 'draft'),
  ('22681126-952e-59e5-97e2-12d780e48738', 'f02fa743-710e-5e6c-880b-e826a6c0056a', 'Fue clausurado, fueron rescatados', 'The headline verb agrees with what it''s about: **el boliche fue clausurado**, **la obra fue clausurada**, **los vecinos fueron rescatados**, **las vecinas fueron rescatadas**. Whoever did it comes after **por**: *por los bomberos*.', 'draft'),
  ('27c30a60-8fbf-5356-81aa-cc1f86051cbc', 'f02fa743-710e-5e6c-880b-e826a6c0056a', 'Hubo un incendio', 'The news opens with **hubo**: **hubo un incendio**, **hubo un accidente en la avenida**, **hubo dos heridos** — who then **fueron trasladados al hospital**. At the kitchen table the same story loses the passive: *trasladaron a los heridos*.', 'draft'),
  ('aeee8169-0182-5de3-b34a-3b61a016548d', 'f02fa743-710e-5e6c-880b-e826a6c0056a', 'Fue elegida', 'Not only bad news: **la pizzería fue elegida la mejor del barrio**, **la ley fue aprobada**, **el chico fue elegido para el equipo**. Same pattern: **fue** + a participle that agrees.', 'draft'),
  ('2a3a2462-0e4e-58df-9bc1-fcf6e909f66e', 'cb40d619-f85d-5762-844a-cf3d5270c3c3', '¿Dónde votás?', 'Election day is a Sunday, and everyone asks **¿dónde votás?** You check the **padrón** — *the voter roll* — for your school and your **mesa**. **Votamos** in the school around the corner; **mi abuela votó a las ocho**, first in line.', 'draft'),
  ('60436255-a5f1-5601-8f69-39f8dd6f913a', 'cb40d619-f85d-5762-844a-cf3d5270c3c3', 'El cuarto oscuro', 'The booth is the **cuarto oscuro** — *the dark room* — where you pick your **boleta** and drop it in the **urna**. The **voto** is secret. If nobody wins outright, there''s a **balotaje** — *a runoff*. Missed it? You have to **justificar** why.', 'draft'),
  ('0f7e9624-af5b-5d2f-a1e1-b521a0dc51c1', 'cb40d619-f85d-5762-844a-cf3d5270c3c3', 'Las encuestas', 'Before, the **campaña**, the **debate** on TV and the **encuestas** — *the polls* — that always get it wrong. After, the **resultado**. The course stays out of who won.', 'draft'),
  ('a7707333-9bed-5180-8835-8a8805c92044', '498e2179-7921-5c4c-8aa0-add0a77bf455', 'Paro docente, hubo un apagón', '**Paro docente**, **suspendieron el servicio**, **hubo desvíos** — and the city **a pie**.', 'draft'),
  ('58fc7f5c-e2ec-5166-8d07-db2fd498b0aa', '498e2179-7921-5c4c-8aa0-add0a77bf455', 'Fue clausurado, ¿dónde votás?', '**Fue clausurado**, **fueron rescatados**: **fue** + a participle that agrees. And on Sunday, **¿dónde votás?**', 'draft'),
  ('6d88948a-49cd-507f-b390-3b282380d755', '3705206f-e1a9-53a2-bcab-add275f67100', 'Según quién', '**Según** takes people as well as papers: **según él**, **según ellos**, **según la fuente**. **Aparentemente** is the neutral *apparently*; **se ve que** is what you conclude from what you see: **se ve que llovió** — *it must have rained*.', 'draft'),
  ('3ff85211-a894-5d45-b66e-973838dc3d86', '3705206f-e1a9-53a2-bcab-add275f67100', 'Lo desmintieron', 'A story is **confirmado** or it''s **desmentido**: **el gremio desmintió el rumor**, **lo desmintieron en el noticiero**. Before you forward it, ask **¿cuál es la fuente?** — the **titular** says one thing, the **versión oficial** another.', 'draft'),
  ('df9ba005-f0db-553b-a492-50b1f5d3f3ce', '3705206f-e1a9-53a2-bcab-add275f67100', 'Me llegó una cadena', 'The family WhatsApp group sends a **cadena** — *a chain message* — every morning. **Chequeá la fuente** before you believe it.', 'draft'),
  ('9f1b4f75-62bb-5fd3-bfb4-117dc43f4612', 'e38a0b51-167e-583b-a179-5eafde3573f0', 'Me afanaron, nos robaron', 'Among friends it''s **me afanaron** — *they nicked it* — with the same *they* that nobody names. It moves with the victim: **te robaron**, **le robaron a mi vieja**, **nos robaron la bici**. The **motochorro** does it from a motorbike.', 'draft'),
  ('68bbdfb3-c560-5eab-a9a4-e53a956ef37d', 'e38a0b51-167e-583b-a179-5eafde3573f0', 'El cuento del tío', '**Me estafaron** — *I got scammed* — is quieter: a call from a fake bank, a **billete trucho**, the **cuento del tío** — *the old con* — on your grandmother. First thing: **bloqueá la tarjeta**. Then the denuncia, with the **cámaras** of the block if you''re lucky.', 'draft'),
  ('a9d44d65-c0ea-523c-a2ec-38cdabf80bdc', 'e38a0b51-167e-583b-a179-5eafde3573f0', 'Me descuidé', 'The confession that comes with it: **me descuidé** — *I let my guard down*. Porteños answer **¡qué garrón!**', 'draft'),
  ('5c59e9dc-914b-5172-9d87-3fa83a52e4b9', '6a58e148-25f1-55f5-9568-c47c2c011c1e', 'Se tapó, se trabó', 'Things at home break on their own, with **se**: **se tapó el inodoro** — *the toilet''s blocked*; **se trabó el ascensor** — *the lift got stuck*; **se cortó el agua**. Nobody did it — it just **se rompió**.', 'draft'),
  ('e7c5b8b2-bd38-57ba-bd75-9d14c7757dc8', '6a58e148-25f1-55f5-9568-c47c2c011c1e', '¿A quién llamo?', 'Each problem has its person: the **plomero** for a **canilla** that **gotea** — *a dripping tap* — the **gasista** for the calefón, the **encargado** for the **portero eléctrico**. A **filtración** from the flat upstairs goes to the **administración**, and takes months.', 'draft'),
  ('dfc1ac34-7548-5d02-be4a-02938c07fce4', 'e4860d3e-3ee3-5fc4-8b35-41209dd58a5e', 'Aparentemente, se ve que', '**Aparentemente**, **se ve que**, **lo desmintieron** — and always **¿cuál es la fuente?**', 'draft'),
  ('cab9d500-1ea5-50a6-b22b-98ddbe3c2137', 'e4860d3e-3ee3-5fc4-8b35-41209dd58a5e', 'Me afanaron, se tapó', '**Me afanaron la billetera**, **me estafaron**; **se tapó la canilla**, **se trabó el ascensor** — the *they* nobody names, and the *se* nobody did.', 'draft'),
  ('221c8d0b-ad2b-59ef-9e73-229943384be9', 'f1ea7582-a6b4-56df-99dc-3dd945f9d0f9', 'Hinchamos por el mismo', '**Hinchar por** runs in the family: **en casa hinchamos todos por el mismo cuadro**; **de chico hinchaba por otro, pero mi viejo no me dejó**. A fan **de toda la vida** never changes club — changing wife is easier, they say.', 'draft'),
  ('bcc20295-b0f0-5657-8bba-544e8abc8f78', 'f1ea7582-a6b4-56df-99dc-3dd945f9d0f9', 'Ser socio', 'To go to the **estadio** you''re **socio** — *a member* — of the **club**, and pay the cuota. The **hinchada** sings its **cantitos** for ninety minutes, under the **banderas**. Away fans? Banned for years: you only go **de visitante** on TV.', 'draft'),
  ('8025b919-8dbc-5168-8231-8ae8acf126fb', 'f1ea7582-a6b4-56df-99dc-3dd945f9d0f9', 'El ídolo', 'Every club has its **ídolo**, the **jugador** whose shirt the kids wear. And every fan fears one word: the **descenso** — *relegation*.', 'draft'),
  ('5a5e8f75-3fbb-503c-ab9a-371872ba6b24', '85347a66-3161-5a8d-9251-44225d44ad33', 'Tocar, cantar, bailar', 'An instrument is **tocar**: **¿tocás la guitarra?**, **mi abuelo tocaba el bandoneón en una orquesta**. **¿Cantás?** **¿Bailás tango?** — and at the milonga, **¿bailamos?**', 'draft'),
  ('968d241f-9d2a-5644-9eff-acf620874f77', '85347a66-3161-5a8d-9251-44225d44ad33', 'No todo es tango', 'Porteños grew up on **rock nacional** — *Argentine rock* — sung in Spanish in the stadiums; the provinces on **folclore**; every party ends in **cumbia**. A **cantante** is a singer; the one who sings tango is a *cantor*.', 'draft'),
  ('63d225c6-fc98-5274-a78a-5cfab143c80e', '85347a66-3161-5a8d-9251-44225d44ad33', 'Piazzolla', 'Astor **Piazzolla** took the tango out of the **pista** — *the dance floor* — and into the concert hall. The old milongueros never forgave him.', 'draft'),
  ('320ccab5-810e-5019-b4e8-625dde6a8ac3', '02841028-7fa9-5c47-9159-c4b47cc15cc1', 'La parrillada', 'For the table there''s the **parrillada** — *a mixed grill* on its own little grill: chorizo, morcilla, **mollejas**, **chinchulines** and a **tira de asado**. On your own: a **bife de chorizo** or an **entraña**.', 'draft'),
  ('56f2eb46-cd35-5649-9776-16424039e6cd', '02841028-7fa9-5c47-9159-c4b47cc15cc1', '¿Y la salsa?', 'On the table: **chimichurri** — oil, garlic, parsley, chilli — and **salsa criolla** — onion, tomato, pepper. Ketchup is a crime. The meat is cooked **a la leña** at the good places.', 'draft'),
  ('d9075515-9557-5e2e-986b-a39b62161f51', '02841028-7fa9-5c47-9159-c4b47cc15cc1', 'Bien cocido', 'Jugosa, a punto, or **bien cocido** — *well done*; **vuelta y vuelta** is barely warm. The bill has a line for the **cubierto** — *the cover charge*: the bread and the cutlery.', 'draft'),
  ('48b85097-326c-51e1-99e2-9b7f15b7a5a2', '013dc4ab-e838-53ac-ac0a-48d708431761', 'Socio de toda la vida', '**Socio del club**, **hincha de toda la vida**, the **hinchada** and its **cantitos**.', 'draft'),
  ('58e4762c-bf6a-52ff-96cb-4266d6ed8a4e', '013dc4ab-e838-53ac-ac0a-48d708431761', 'Rock, cumbia y parrillada', '**¿Tocás la guitarra?** **¿Bailás?** And after, a **parrillada** with **chimichurri**, the meat **bien cocido** or jugoso.', 'draft'),
  ('15cf0e24-29ae-5afb-a07d-7d43ebcff091', 'c18ed3f6-ae4d-50fd-b360-6d7e7d73144c', 'Lo lindo, lo feo', 'Put **lo** in front of an adjective and it becomes *the … thing*: **lo lindo** — *the nice thing*; **lo feo** — *the ugly part*; **lo difícil** — *the hard part*; **lo único** — *the only thing*: **lo único que extraño es el mar**.', 'draft'),
  ('a75b10b9-a779-55fa-ae70-312528aa56c8', 'c18ed3f6-ae4d-50fd-b360-6d7e7d73144c', 'Lo más lindo', '**Lo más** + adjective is *the most … thing*: **lo más lindo del barrio es la plaza**. Weighing it up, porteños say the city **tiene sus cosas** — *has its issues*: the **inseguridad**, the **costo de vida** — but the **calidad de vida**, **a la vez**, is hard to beat.', 'draft')
